  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1254 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nWednesday through Monday:\n\nStrong high pressure centered just north of the eastern Great \nLakes early Wednesday will largely remain in place the second\nhalf of the week while gradually weakening. Meanwhile, upper\nlevel ridging will attempt to build in from the west through\nlate week. Models still differ as to whether southern Wisconsin\nwill be more under the influence of the departing troughing\npattern or the approaching ridge by the end of the week into the\nweekend. Thus there remains some uncertainty with temps during\nthis period, though an overall slight warming trend looks\nlikely. Additionally, models suggest a shortwave may come over \nthe top of the ridge late week or during the weekend, bringing\nshower chances back to the area. As with temps, there is still \nuncertainty with the timing of any precip given the differences \nwith the trough/ridge among models.\n\nDDV",
